      <workList xml:id="workDesc_246fb9ef">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e219216">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_5d53f49d">A1:103</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_7a057bbe" xml:lang="it">Concerto IV</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_069c8680">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_5623da05">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_cfa8461e">
               <p xml:id="idm130">According to the entry of the Breitkopf catalogue of 1761, the present concerto is for harpsichord obligato, two flutes and strings; however, in the publishers' catalogue issued two years later the instrumentation indicated excludes the flutes. The incipit provided in the second catalogue reveals that the incomplete copy of the harpsichord part in Uppsala is part of this concerto. The physical evidence of the transcript suggests that the part material was produced sometime during the second half of the eighteenth century by a professional or an experienced copyist – most likely the Breitkopf publishers. The style of the music, however, indicates that it was one of Scheibe's early works. According to the harpsichord part, the concerto was part of a larger collection of which this one was numbered 6. The part shows signs of wear. See also introduction to SchW A1:Coll.001.</p>
            </history>
